{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016zTXYf8911AAXLzAttEZDq","type":"tool_result","content":"# Plan for #43\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n\nThis plan was supplied by a maintainer PR (the trusted channel), because the issue as filed names protected `.ard/reviewers/` paths. It covers the starter role only (part A). Where the issue body and this plan differ, follow this plan.\n\nShip the starter role `reviewers/security-review` in `internal/roles/` (embedded for `ard init`), like `reviewers/eng-review` (#36). A role exists because its directory exists: `internal/roles/roles.go` already embeds `reviewers`, so the new prompt is picked up by `ard init` and `config.LoadFS` with no Go behaviour change. The reviewer loop, close-out contract, findings schema and posting are generic and stay untouched.\n\nOwner decisions (2026-11-23):\n\n- The #42 dependency is dropped. The role has no `when:`; the starter worker leaves `reviewers` unset, so it requests every reviewer role. If #42 merges first, rebase and keep `When == nil` in the load test.\n- A missing tool is skipped: say so in `## Checks` and review by reading. Never `needs-human` for a missing tool.\n- Network: the #36 rule. The package manager may fetch declared dependencies, nothing else. No semgrep registry or `auto` configs, no vulnerability-database lookups (known CVEs stay with the cve scanner).\n- A medium finding blocks when it is one of the four kinds (injection, authz, secret, dependency) and the reviewer can name how it would be exploited. Critical and high always block; low and info never.\n- The role is static only: it never builds, tests or runs the repository's code (unlike eng-review).\n- Each finding's first line starts with a kind tag: `[injection]`, `[authz]`, `[secret]`, `[dependency]` or `[other]`.\n- Planted-issue fixtures are not committed: the owner runs the smoke test by hand on a scratch module outside the repo.\n\nBoundaries for the worker:\n\n- Do not edit anything under `.ard/` (role directories, `.ard/config.yaml`) except your own report; the diff guard holds the job. Ard's own `.ard/` gets this role in a later owner PR.\n- Do not edit `CLAUDE.md` beyond step 8 below. It is in `merge.protected_paths`, so that one-line layout edit needs a human approval; say so in your report.\n- Edit no non-test Go code other than the doc comment named in step 3. No change to `internal/reviewer`, `internal/closeout`, `internal/agent`, `internal/config` or `internal/initcmd` non-test files.\n\nIf #41 has already changed `internal/roles/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt` on your base (previous findings in round 2 and later), mirror that change in this prompt and in its shape test.\n\nFiles:\n\n1. **`internal/roles/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt`** (new): the prompt below. ASCII only, at most 16 KiB (the draft is 15,797 bytes; if tuning needs room, raise the test cap and say why, rather than dropping rules). Wording may be tuned, but keep every rule and every string the tests check.\n2. **`internal/roles/config.yaml`**: after the `reviewers/eng-review` line add `reviewers/security-review: { model: claude-opus-5-5 }`. Default timeout (30m), no `when:`. Leave `workers/engineer.reviewers` unset.\n3. **`internal/roles/roles.go`**: the doc comment of `FS`: the role list becomes \"scanners/cve, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review and reviewers/security-review\". The embed line is unchanged.\n4. **`internal/roles/roles_test.go`**: `TestFSContents` want list: add `\"reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\"` right after `\"reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\"`.\n5. **`internal/roles/eng_review_test.go`**: in `TestEmbeddedEngReviewLoadsAsReviewer`, replace the `len(rs) != 1 || rs[0].Name != \"eng-review\"` check with `strings.Join(reviewerNames(res), \",\") != \"eng-review,security-review\"`, and update the comment: the starter worker requests every reviewer role, so both run on every green PR.\n6. **`internal/roles/security_review_test.go`** (new): the four tests under Test plan. It defines `reviewerNames`, used by both files. Reuse the package's `starterFS`, `stubRoles`, `fencedFrontmatter`, `hasLabel` and `reviewJob`; do not redefine them.\n7. **`internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go`**: `starterTree`: add `.ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt` after the eng-review entry. The PR-body list (around line 193): add the same path. The label list (around line 216): add `labels.Request(labels.StageReview, \"security-review\")`, `labels.Running(...)`, `labels.Done(...)` and `labels.Changes(\"security-review\")`.\n8. **`CLAUDE.md`**: Layout, the `internal/roles/` line with the role list: append `reviewers/security-review`. (Human approval needed.)\n9. **`docs/proposal.md`**: see Proposal edits below.\n\n#### Facts the prompt must match\n\n- Invocation: stage `review`; the user message names the role and lists `Spec.Untrusted` = `[.ard-input/N/diff.patch, .ard-input/N/issue.md, .ard-input/N/comments.md, .ard/N]`. Tools: `Read,Glob,Grep,Edit,Write,Bash`. `$ARD_SIDECAR` is set when the role has a sidecar; `$ARD_ROLE_DIR` always is (unused by the starter).\n- Role file: `.ard/N/review-security-review.md` (`agent.RoleFilePath(n, \"review\", \"security-review\")`); `role: security-review`; `status` `done` or `needs-human`; `verdict` required when done; `findings` with `file` (quoted, relative), `line` (int >= 1), `severity` (critical, high, medium, low or info), `blocking` (bool) and `message` (a block scalar). At most `closeout.MaxFindings` (50). No `next` and no `worker` key.\n- Posting: a finding on a `+` line goes inline; anything else goes in the body with the first line cut to 300 runes. An approve with a blocking finding becomes changes.\n\n#### Prompt (`internal/roles/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt`)\n\nSections in order: opening (with the four kinds), inputs, `## Trust`, `## What you may do`, `## Steps`, `## Checks`, `## Findings`, `## The format of review-security-review.md`, `## Examples`. Write the text between the outer fences, byte for byte as a starting point:\n\ninternal/roles:\nconfig.yaml\ncve_docker_integration_test.go\ncve_integration_test.go\ncve_test.go\ndocs_docker_integration_test.go\ndocs_test.go\neng_review_test.go\nengineer_test.go\nerrcodes_integration_test.go\nerrcodes_test.go\nlead_test.go\nreviewers\nroles.go\nroles_test.go\nscanners\ntestdata\ntriage\nworker_engineer_test.go\nworkers\n\ninternal/roles/reviewers/eng-review:\nprompt.txt\n# ard configuration, proposed by `ard init`. Edit freely; this file is yours.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/docs: { every: 3d, max_open: 3, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/error-codes: { every: 24h, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  # timeout covers the whole worker job (agent, tests, fix rounds). tests is your\n  # repo's test command; \"\" turns the test step off.\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\ninternal/roles/roles.go:10:// directories (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer and reviewers/eng-review); paths are relative to .ard/.\ninternal/roles/roles_test.go:32:\twant := []string{\"config.yaml\", \"reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \"scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\", \"triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \"workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\ninternal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go:145:var starterTree = []string{\".ard/config.yaml\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \".ard/scanners/docs/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\ninternal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go:200:\tfor _, s := range []string{\"bot-commits.yml\", \"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\", \"Squash and merge\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\"} {\ninternal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go:230:\tfor _, want := range []string{labels.Running(labels.StageTriage, \"lead\"), labels.Done(labels.StageTriage, \"lead\"), \"ard:triage:engineer\", labels.Running(labels.StageTriage, \"engineer\"), labels.Done(labels.StageTriage, \"engineer\"), labels.Request(labels.StageWorker, \"engineer\"), labels.Running(labels.StageWorker, \"engineer\"), labels.Done(labels.StageWorker, \"engineer\"), labels.Request(labels.StageReview, \"eng-review\"), labels.Running(labels.StageReview, \"eng-review\"), labels.Done(labels.StageReview, \"eng-review\"), labels.Changes(\"eng-review\")} {\nCLAUDE.md:54:internal/roles/     starter role directories embedded for ard init (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review)\ndocs/proposal.md:140:next: [review:security-review, review:eng-review]   # optional requests\ndocs/proposal.md:331:**The starter reviewer (`reviewers/eng-review`, #36).** `.ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt` checks correctness, missing tests and drift from `plan.md`. Its inputs, all untrusted, are `diff.patch`, `issue.md`, `comments.md` and the committed `.ard/<issue#>/`; text in the change that addresses a reviewer is a blocking `high` finding on its line (verdict `changes`), and the same text in the issue, comments or `.ard/<issue#>/` is ignored and mentioned in the body. It runs the repository's own linter and the changed packages' tests with coverage through Bash, writing scratch files outside the worktree, reports only problems on added lines and skips a check it cannot run, saying so; the package manager may fetch declared dependencies and nothing else is downloaded. Critical and high findings always block, medium only when it is a real bug, low and info never; a missing test blocks only when it is `high` (risky or core logic, or a case `plan.md` named), smaller gaps are `medium`. The verdict is `changes` exactly when a finding blocks. `line` is the head-side line: a `+` line goes inline, anything else in the body. It writes only `review-eng-review.md` with `role: eng-review`, `attempt: 1`, `status` `done` or `needs-human`, `findings` with a double-quoted `file` and a `message: |` block, never `next` or `worker`, and a body with a `## Checks` section. It answers `needs-human` only when there is nothing to review or the issue and the plan contradict each other. The starter override is Sonnet 5.5 with the default 30m timeout and no `when:`, so every PR from the starter worker gets it. It ships no Dockerfile, so it runs as a host subprocess with the #84 warning until #55.\ndocs/proposal.md:340:| eng-review | always | lint and coverage of added lines (the repo's own commands, run by the agent) | correctness, missing tests, drift from `plan.md` |\ndocs/proposal.md:415:  workers/engineer:         { tests: make test, timeout: 60m, reviewers: [security-review, eng-review] }\ndocs/proposal.md:424:**`ard init` proposes the starter `.ard/` as a PR (decided, #27).** It builds `config.yaml` and the starter roles in memory (today `scanners/cve`, `scanners/docs`, `scanners/error-codes`, `triage/lead`, `triage/engineer`, `workers/engineer` and `reviewers/eng-review`; `intake: {mode: label}`, the protected-path defaults above, and the cve, docs, error-codes, lead, engineer, worker and eng-review overrides), compares them with `main`, commits them on a new branch `ard-init` cut from `main` through the effect layer and a narrow committer lane, pushes it and opens a PR. It writes nothing to the local working tree or to `main`, and `scan` is committed `100755`. Files that already exist on `main` with different contents are a conflict naming the paths; `--force` proposes overwriting them, and init never deletes anything. It refuses while `ard-init` exists on the remote, whatever its PR's state, so it never force-pushes over or stacks commits on a human's edits: merge or close the PR, delete the branch and rerun. If `main` already has every starter file it prints `nothing to propose`. It syncs the label catalogue first (like `ard labels sync`), so a failure leaves nothing pushed. With `--dry-run` the commit, push and PR are logged to the ledger instead of acting. A missing repo, credentials or `main` branch exits 1 with nothing written, and `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` auth is refused outside `--dry-run`. The PR body carries the one step the App cannot do: copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` and set the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (optionally `ARD_BOT_CHECK_SINCE`). It also says to merge with **Squash and merge** or **Create a merge commit**, never a fast-forward from the command line, which would put the bot's commit on main's first-parent history. **Rebase and merge** is also safe: the scratch-repo run (#85) showed GitHub records the merging human as committer of a rebase-merged commit (the bot stays the author), and the bot-commit check keys on committer, so it does not flag it. The body still names only the two merges above.\ndocs/proposal.md:485:    P0[\"Phase 0: Skeleton<br/>controller and config<br/>label bootstrap<br/>committer, local executor<br/>cve and stale scanners<br/>dry-run mode\"] -->|\"Gate 1: 1 week dry-run, 0 duplicate issues\"| P1[\"Phase 1: First loop<br/>lead + engineer triage<br/>engineer worker<br/>eng-review<br/>Reaper<br/>human approval gate\"]\ninternal/roles/eng_review_test.go:21:func reviewJob() closeout.Job {\ninternal/roles/lead_test.go:17:type stubRoles map[config.Kind][]string\ninternal/roles/lead_test.go:88:func fencedFrontmatter(prompt string) []string {\ninternal/roles/roles_test.go:148:func starterFS(t *testing.T, chmod bool) fstest.MapFS {\ninternal/roles/worker_engineer_test.go:160:func hasLabel(ls []closeout.Label, want closeout.Label) bool {\nf360928 Rewrite #215 plan to incorporate review amendments and owner answers (#233)\nb957db1 ard(worker:engineer): #212 Adds the standalone Go helper of the missing-tests scanner, with fixtur… [skip ci]\ne516867 Scanner: docs — undocumented exported Go identifiers (#51) (#228)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0a16640-e701-4bfd-9d33-042dad4ed6b9","uuid":"a966cf47-9f55-4433-9f2c-1d68503f2a31","timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:35:53.686Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Plan for #43\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n\nThis plan was supplied by a maintainer PR (the trusted channel), because the issue as filed names protected `.ard/reviewers/` paths. It covers the starter role only (part A). Where the issue body and this plan differ, follow this plan.\n\nShip the starter role `reviewers/security-review` in `internal/roles/` (embedded for `ard init`), like `reviewers/eng-review` (#36). A role exists because its directory exists: `internal/roles/roles.go` already embeds `reviewers`, so the new prompt is picked up by `ard init` and `config.LoadFS` with no Go behaviour change. The reviewer loop, close-out contract, findings schema and posting are generic and stay untouched.\n\nOwner decisions (2026-11-23):\n\n- The #42 dependency is dropped. The role has no `when:`; the starter worker leaves `reviewers` unset, so it requests every reviewer role. If #42 merges first, rebase and keep `When == nil` in the load test.\n- A missing tool is skipped: say so in `## Checks` and review by reading. Never `needs-human` for a missing tool.\n- Network: the #36 rule. The package manager may fetch declared dependencies, nothing else. No semgrep registry or `auto` configs, no vulnerability-database lookups (known CVEs stay with the cve scanner).\n- A medium finding blocks when it is one of the four kinds (injection, authz, secret, dependency) and the reviewer can name how it would be exploited. Critical and high always block; low and info never.\n- The role is static only: it never builds, tests or runs the repository's code (unlike eng-review).\n- Each finding's first line starts with a kind tag: `[injection]`, `[authz]`, `[secret]`, `[dependency]` or `[other]`.\n- Planted-issue fixtures are not committed: the owner runs the smoke test by hand on a scratch module outside the repo.\n\nBoundaries for the worker:\n\n- Do not edit anything under `.ard/` (role directories, `.ard/config.yaml`) except your own report; the diff guard holds the job. Ard's own `.ard/` gets this role in a later owner PR.\n- Do not edit `CLAUDE.md` beyond step 8 below. It is in `merge.protected_paths`, so that one-line layout edit needs a human approval; say so in your report.\n- Edit no non-test Go code other than the doc comment named in step 3. No change to `internal/reviewer`, `internal/closeout`, `internal/agent`, `internal/config` or `internal/initcmd` non-test files.\n\nIf #41 has already changed `internal/roles/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt` on your base (previous findings in round 2 and later), mirror that change in this prompt and in its shape test.\n\nFiles:\n\n1. **`internal/roles/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt`** (new): the prompt below. ASCII only, at most 16 KiB (the draft is 15,797 bytes; if tuning needs room, raise the test cap and say why, rather than dropping rules). Wording may be tuned, but keep every rule and every string the tests check.\n2. **`internal/roles/config.yaml`**: after the `reviewers/eng-review` line add `reviewers/security-review: { model: claude-opus-5-5 }`. Default timeout (30m), no `when:`. Leave `workers/engineer.reviewers` unset.\n3. **`internal/roles/roles.go`**: the doc comment of `FS`: the role list becomes \"scanners/cve, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review and reviewers/security-review\". The embed line is unchanged.\n4. **`internal/roles/roles_test.go`**: `TestFSContents` want list: add `\"reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\"` right after `\"reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\"`.\n5. **`internal/roles/eng_review_test.go`**: in `TestEmbeddedEngReviewLoadsAsReviewer`, replace the `len(rs) != 1 || rs[0].Name != \"eng-review\"` check with `strings.Join(reviewerNames(res), \",\") != \"eng-review,security-review\"`, and update the comment: the starter worker requests every reviewer role, so both run on every green PR.\n6. **`internal/roles/security_review_test.go`** (new): the four tests under Test plan. It defines `reviewerNames`, used by both files. Reuse the package's `starterFS`, `stubRoles`, `fencedFrontmatter`, `hasLabel` and `reviewJob`; do not redefine them.\n7. **`internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go`**: `starterTree`: add `.ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt` after the eng-review entry. The PR-body list (around line 193): add the same path. The label list (around line 216): add `labels.Request(labels.StageReview, \"security-review\")`, `labels.Running(...)`, `labels.Done(...)` and `labels.Changes(\"security-review\")`.\n8. **`CLAUDE.md`**: Layout, the `internal/roles/` line with the role list: append `reviewers/security-review`. (Human approval needed.)\n9. **`docs/proposal.md`**: see Proposal edits below.\n\n#### Facts the prompt must match\n\n- Invocation: stage `review`; the user message names the role and lists `Spec.Untrusted` = `[.ard-input/N/diff.patch, .ard-input/N/issue.md, .ard-input/N/comments.md, .ard/N]`. Tools: `Read,Glob,Grep,Edit,Write,Bash`. `$ARD_SIDECAR` is set when the role has a sidecar; `$ARD_ROLE_DIR` always is (unused by the starter).\n- Role file: `.ard/N/review-security-review.md` (`agent.RoleFilePath(n, \"review\", \"security-review\")`); `role: security-review`; `status` `done` or `needs-human`; `verdict` required when done; `findings` with `file` (quoted, relative), `line` (int >= 1), `severity` (critical, high, medium, low or info), `blocking` (bool) and `message` (a block scalar). At most `closeout.MaxFindings` (50). No `next` and no `worker` key.\n- Posting: a finding on a `+` line goes inline; anything else goes in the body with the first line cut to 300 runes. An approve with a blocking finding becomes changes.\n\n#### Prompt (`internal/roles/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt`)\n\nSections in order: opening (with the four kinds), inputs, `## Trust`, `## What you may do`, `## Steps`, `## Checks`, `## Findings`, `## The format of review-security-review.md`, `## Examples`. Write the text between the outer fences, byte for byte as a starting point:\n\ninternal/roles:\nconfig.yaml\ncve_docker_integration_test.go\ncve_integration_test.go\ncve_test.go\ndocs_docker_integration_test.go\ndocs_test.go\neng_review_test.go\nengineer_test.go\nerrcodes_integration_test.go\nerrcodes_test.go\nlead_test.go\nreviewers\nroles.go\nroles_test.go\nscanners\ntestdata\ntriage\nworker_engineer_test.go\nworkers\n\ninternal/roles/reviewers/eng-review:\nprompt.txt\n# ard configuration, proposed by `ard init`. Edit freely; this file is yours.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/docs: { every: 3d, max_open: 3, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/error-codes: { every: 24h, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  # timeout covers the whole worker job (agent, tests, fix rounds). tests is your\n  # repo's test command; \"\" turns the test step off.\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\ninternal/roles/roles.go:10:// directories (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer and reviewers/eng-review); paths are relative to .ard/.\ninternal/roles/roles_test.go:32:\twant := []string{\"config.yaml\", \"reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \"scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\", \"triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \"workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\ninternal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go:145:var starterTree = []string{\".ard/config.yaml\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \".ard/scanners/docs/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\ninternal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go:200:\tfor _, s := range []string{\"bot-commits.yml\", \"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\", \"Squash and merge\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\"} {\ninternal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go:230:\tfor _, want := range []string{labels.Running(labels.StageTriage, \"lead\"), labels.Done(labels.StageTriage, \"lead\"), \"ard:triage:engineer\", labels.Running(labels.StageTriage, \"engineer\"), labels.Done(labels.StageTriage, \"engineer\"), labels.Request(labels.StageWorker, \"engineer\"), labels.Running(labels.StageWorker